.TH CVECTOR_GET_MPROCS 3 "2026-09-20" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_get_mprocs \- get the memory management procedures of a vector
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *cvector_get_mprocs(cvec v);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the memory management procedures that the vector allocates
through. Code that gets an existing vector can therefore allocate
scratch storage from the same allocator that the vector uses.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to query
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a pointer to the memory management procedures of the vector
Returns NULL when the caller created the vector with the default
allocator. That is the case when the mmgmt_procs argument of
cvector_create_full() was NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
A NULL return is not an error. It means "use the defaults of the
library". Every routine in the library that takes a
ccol_memmgmt_procs_t * accepts NULL with exactly that meaning
The vector owns the structure. The library frees the structure when it
destroys the vector. Do not free the structure yourself
Asserts if v is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_create_full (3),
.BR cvec_sort (3),
.BR cvector_destroy (3)
